      "message": "That\u0027s true for the outer manifest. \nFor a submanifest, `XmlManifest.__init__()` then adjusts `topdir`:\n```\nself.topdir \u003d os.path.dirname(self.repodir)\nif submanifest_path:\n    self.topdir \u003d os.path.join(self.topdir, submanifest_path)\n```\nSubmanifests still share the same `repodir`, so for one at `sub`:\n```\ndirname(manifest.repodir) \u003d \u003croot\u003e\nmanifest.topdir           \u003d \u003croot\u003e/sub\n```\n`LocalSyncState` now stores `Project.RelPath(local\u003dFalse)`, for example `sub/proj`. \nCombining that with the submanifest `topdir` would produce `\u003croot\u003e/sub/sub/proj` instead of `\u003croot\u003e/sub/proj`.\n\n`dirname(repodir)` does give the right base here, but I agree it\u0027s not obvious why. \nI\u0027ve already switched it to `self._manifest.outer_client.topdir`, to make that explicit.",
